WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.033
Gym.

2
00:00:01.313 --> 00:00:05.643
Day 44 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.393 --> 00:00:08.417
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.697 --> 00:00:18.361
Today's goal: join a gym, talk to a trainer about your goals and health, ask about equipment, and use gym etiquette, like sharing machines and asking for a spot.

5
00:00:19.711 --> 00:00:20.565
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:21.805
Key words.

7
00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:24.399
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:47.633
Word or phrase, and Meaning. membership (monthly or quarterly or annual): the plan you pay for. personal trainer (PT) / trainer: coach. warm-up or cool-down or stretching: before or after exercise. cardio (treadmill, cycle, cross-trainer): heart exercise. weights or dumbbells or barbell or machines: strength equipment. sets and reps:

9
00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:56.660
3 sets of 12 reps. form or posture: the correct way to do an exercise. spot (someone): stand by to help with a heavy lift.

10
00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.319
sore or pulled a muscle or sprain: pain after exercise or injury.

11
00:01:03.669 --> 00:01:04.544
Part 2.

12
00:01:04.824 --> 00:01:06.040
Questions you'll ask.

13
00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.079
Joining.

14
00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:10.109
What membership plans do you have?

15
00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:11.754
Is there a joining fee?

16
00:01:12.034 --> 00:01:13.186
What are the timings?

17
00:01:13.466 --> 00:01:15.002
Is it open on Sundays?

18
00:01:15.282 --> 00:01:17.607
Is a trainer included, or is that extra?

19
00:01:17.887 --> 00:01:19.893
Can I try one free session first?

20
00:01:20.173 --> 00:01:22.413
Can I freeze my membership if I travel?

21
00:01:23.763 --> 00:01:24.744
With the trainer.

22
00:01:25.024 --> 00:01:28.352
I want to lose weight or build strength or improve stamina.

23
00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:29.784
What do you suggest?

24
00:01:30.064 --> 00:01:31.579
I have knee or back pain.

25
00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:33.736
Which exercises should I avoid?

26
00:01:34.016 --> 00:01:35.275
Is my form correct?

27
00:01:35.555 --> 00:01:37.347
How many sets and reps should I do?

28
00:01:37.627 --> 00:01:39.888
What should I eat before and after a workout?

29
00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:42.326
On the gym floor.

30
00:01:42.606 --> 00:01:46.126
Are you using this machine? / How many sets do you have left?

31
00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.665
Can I work in with you?

32
00:01:47.945 --> 00:01:49.566
(share the machine between sets).

33
00:01:49.846 --> 00:01:51.147
Could you spot me, please?

34
00:01:51.427 --> 00:01:53.347
Could you show me how to adjust this seat?

35
00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:55.593
Part 3.

36
00:01:55.873 --> 00:01:58.071
Conversation 1: joining the gym.

37
00:01:59.321 --> 00:02:01.347
Here is how the conversation goes.

38
00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:02.417
Hi!

39
00:02:02.697 --> 00:02:04.105
Welcome to FitZone.

40
00:02:04.385 --> 00:02:05.643
How can I help you?

41
00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:06.649
Hi.

42
00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:08.657
I'd like to join the gym.

43
00:02:08.937 --> 00:02:10.473
What plans do you have?

44
00:02:10.753 --> 00:02:16.982
Monthly is 2,000, rupeesquarterly is 5,000, rupeesand annual is 15,000 rupees.

45
00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:18.905
Is there a joining fee?

46
00:02:19.185 --> 00:02:20.422
Not this month.

47
00:02:20.702 --> 00:02:21.854
We have an offer.

48
00:02:23.204 --> 00:02:24.804
The conversation continues.

49
00:02:25.084 --> 00:02:26.641
Does it include a trainer?

50
00:02:26.921 --> 00:02:28.820
A general trainer is included.

51
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.300
A personal trainer is 6,000 rupeesextra per month.

52
00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.519
Okay.

53
00:02:33.799 --> 00:02:36.999
Can I try one free session before I decide?

54
00:02:37.279 --> 00:02:39.412
Sure, come tomorrow at 7 am.

55
00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.548
Bring sports shoes and a towel.

56
00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.575
Great.

57
00:02:42.855 --> 00:02:44.775
What are the timings on Sundays?

58
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:47.725
The conversation continues.

59
00:02:48.005 --> 00:02:49.903
7 am to 12 noon.

60
00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:51.079
Perfect.

61
00:02:51.359 --> 00:02:52.746
See you tomorrow.

62
00:02:54.096 --> 00:02:55.013
Part 4.

63
00:02:55.293 --> 00:02:58.067
Conversation 2: first session with the trainer.

64
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.343
Here is how the conversation goes.

65
00:03:01.623 --> 00:03:02.861
So, what's your goal?

66
00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:06.021
I want to lose about eight kilos and get fitter.

67
00:03:06.301 --> 00:03:08.199
I sit at a desk all day.

68
00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:09.482
Got it.

69
00:03:09.762 --> 00:03:11.725
Any injuries or health problems?

70
00:03:12.005 --> 00:03:15.781
I have some lower back pain sometimes, and I'm a bit stiff.

71
00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:18.429
Okay, we'll avoid heavy deadlifts for now.

72
00:03:18.709 --> 00:03:21.247
We'll start with a 10-minute warm-up on the treadmill.

73
00:03:22.597 --> 00:03:24.197
The conversation continues.

74
00:03:24.477 --> 00:03:26.632
How many days a week should I come?

75
00:03:26.912 --> 00:03:30.133
Four days to start: two days strength, two days cardio.

76
00:03:30.413 --> 00:03:31.224
Later

77
00:03:31.504 --> 00:03:33.872
Now, three sets of twelve on the leg press.

78
00:03:34.152 --> 00:03:35.773
Is my form correct?

79
00:03:36.053 --> 00:03:37.696
I feel it in my knees.

80
00:03:39.046 --> 00:03:40.646
The conversation continues.

81
00:03:40.926 --> 00:03:43.465
Keep your feet a little higher, and don't lock your knees.

82
00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:45.003
Yes, that's better.

83
00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:46.094
Thanks.

84
00:03:46.374 --> 00:03:48.059
Should I stretch after this?

85
00:03:48.339 --> 00:03:51.070
Yes, always cool down and stretch for five minutes.

86
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.380
Part 5.

87
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.068
Gym etiquette phrases.

88
00:03:56.318 --> 00:03:58.451
Mind if I use this bench while you rest?

89
00:03:58.731 --> 00:04:00.758
Sorry, are you done with these dumbbells?

90
00:04:01.038 --> 00:04:02.617
Could you wipe the machine, please?

91
00:04:02.897 --> 00:04:05.457
(politely) / Let me wipe it down for you.

92
00:04:05.737 --> 00:04:07.699
I'll be quick, only one more set.

93
00:04:09.049 --> 00:04:09.988
Part 6.

94
00:04:10.268 --> 00:04:11.441
When things go wrong.

95
00:04:12.691 --> 00:04:14.825
I think I've pulled a muscle in my shoulder.

96
00:04:15.105 --> 00:04:16.449
Do you have an ice pack?

97
00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:18.222
This treadmill isn't working.

98
00:04:18.502 --> 00:04:19.931
The belt keeps stopping.

99
00:04:20.211 --> 00:04:22.686
I want to cancel or freeze my membership.

100
00:04:22.966 --> 00:04:24.161
What's the process?

101
00:04:25.511 --> 00:04:26.449
Part 7.

102
00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:27.647
Practice.

103
00:04:28.897 --> 00:04:34.102
Tell a trainer your goal, your health issue, and how many days you can come, in 3 sentences.

104
00:04:35.452 --> 00:04:36.327
Part 8.

105
00:04:36.607 --> 00:04:37.652
Speak today.

106
00:04:38.902 --> 00:04:41.611
Say your fitness goal in one clear English sentence.

107
00:04:41.891 --> 00:04:45.390
Learn the questions for sharing a machine and asking for a spot.

108
00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.276
That's the end of this lesson.

109
00:04:48.556 --> 00:04:53.207
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

110
00:04:53.487 --> 00:04:59.609
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

